# Day 19

**17km / 6 hours**

This was a bit of a slower day, owing to the relatively shorter distance but longish time. It began a bit late due to needing to catch a boat across the harbour followed by some decent beach walking.

![A nice shell I found on the beach before returning it to the sand.](./shell.jpg)

![The view of the beach, surely not another one](./beach.jpg)

There was a surprisingly deep river to cross along the beach but the main reason for the slow day was taking a small detour into the town for a proper lunch and some shopping for supplies. 

The boat ride was enjoyable enough, featuring a small detour to look at a small island with seals and birds resting on it. Was a short ride across though, felt like there could be a better way. After finishing the beach walk and camping at the site, I actually went for a short splash in the sea. I would say swim but it wasn't worthy of the term.